import { LOOKS, type Shot } from '../cutscenes';
import { look, own, person, type HeroStory } from './kit';

// Kael, the Oathsworn: squire to Ser Aldric of the Wardens. On the night the star fell the shadow rose out of the Beacon
// Rise; Aldric shoved Kael off the hill, sent his warhorse Cinder after him and shouted “Hold the line where I can’t!”,
// and the shadow took him. Every link of Kael’s story is his own, except the four guardians and Umbra.
//
// I · Sunpetal Meadow: Kael wakes in Farmer Bram’s hay at Millbrook. He follows Cinder’s tracks back to Aldric’s split
//     shield in the reeds of Mirror Lake (and remembers the night), builds Bram a Warden fence, finds Aldric’s book in
//     the saddlebag, fetches the first sun-crystal from Gloom Hollow, where Aldric taught him to be afraid properly, and
//     walks Bram’s boy Wim to Sunpetal to ring the alarm. In Goldenhearth he reports to Brannoc, frees Warden Brin,
//     has Hilda mend the shield, takes the crystals of Rotwood Den (Brin’s old post) and the Sun Shrine (Aldric’s hiding
//     place), calls the muster with the hill fires and catches a boy picking the fallen Wardens’ armour. The shadow has
//     stitched that armour into the Hollow Bulwark; Aldric’s isn’t in it. The muster builds the bridge from Warden oak.
// II · Whisperroot Woods: the old Warden road leads to Thornhold, the Wardens’ lost hall, where the oath-stones show
//     Captain Briarthorn swearing in two squires, Tobb and Aldric, and a rune sleeps under the floor. Kael brings the
//     hall’s watch-horn to Thessaly, runs down the black knight who spares children, walks Old Tobb home, finds the rune
//     young Aldric cut at Blackwater Pool and follows the knight’s frozen trail to the circle where he keeps vigil.
//     Ser Briarthorn, the Oathbreaker, strangles the Bell; Kael breaks him, decides what to do with the old man, and
//     unmakes his thorn wall with a lantern of Bell-bronze.
// III · Starfall Summit: at the Silver Pass the wraith host marches under the Frost Marshal, a wraith wearing the helm
//     Briarthorn threw down. Kael finds a shard for the astronomer, asks the tarn about the helm, holds the pass, lights
//     the Warden fires, is knighted by Brin, forgives a boy who ran (and finds the shard he hid beside), frees the
//     banner-keeper of Skyhold and re-founds the order. The new Wardens melt Umbra’s black ice with three fires of starlight.
// IV · The Ember Wastes: Pyrrhus, the forge-keeper the Wardens forgot, built the Iron Colossus from their melted swords
//     and wanted Aldric for its heart. Kael follows the black knight’s smoking prints, reads the Forge’s mark on his
//     gauntlet, frees old Pyke, finds Aldric at Ashfall Watch, holds the line for him, walks him to the Phoenix Spring,
//     breaks the engine, and keeps his oath when Umbra offers him Aldric’s safety for stepping aside.
const q = own('kael');
const title = (t: string, sub: string, dur = 3.4): Shot => ({ title: t, sub, dur });

